        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>By expressing <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\ln\\left(x^2\\right)]</span> in the form <span class=\"math\">[MATH: k\\ln x,]</span> determine the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: k.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "By expressing [MATH: \\ln\\left(x^2\\right)] in the form [MATH: k\\ln x,] determine the value of [MATH: k.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, let&#x27;s recall the power rule for logarithms:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\log_n(c^m)= m\\log_n\\left( c \\right)]</span></p><p>Using the power rule for logarithms, we get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\ln (x^{2})|= 2\\ln x.]</span></p><p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: k =2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, let's recall the power rule for logarithms:\n\n[MATH: \\log_n(c^m)= m\\log_n\\left( c \\right)]\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms, we get\n[MATH: \\ln (x^{2})|= 2\\ln x.]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: k =2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nBy expressing [MATH: \\ln\\left(x^2\\right)] in the form [MATH: k\\ln x,] determine the value of [MATH: k.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, let's recall the power rule for logarithms:\n\n[MATH: \\log_n(c^m)= m\\log_n\\left( c \\right)]\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms, we get\n[MATH: \\ln (x^{2})|= 2\\ln x.]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: k =2.]"
      },
