          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, let&#x27;s recall the power rule for natural logarithms:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\ln\\left( c^m \\right) = m\\ln{c}]</span></p><p>Using the power rule for logarithms and the information given, we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\ln (x^{3})|= 3 \u22c5 \\ln (x); = 3 \u22c5 0.2; = 0.6.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, let's recall the power rule for natural logarithms:\n[MATH: \\ln\\left( c^m \\right) = m\\ln{c}]\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms and the information given, we get\n\n[MATH: \\ln (x^{3})|= 3 \u22c5 \\ln (x); = 3 \u22c5 0.2; = 0.6.]",
